Subject: Re: trap happy/shy
Message-ID: <gcFRqV1bjOw.uJNVgLGkBwAJ@secrgroup.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <gcFRqV1bjOw.qac5csybBwAJ@secrgroup.groups.google.com>
References: <gcFRqV1bjOw.qac5csybBwAJ@secrgroup.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/secrgroup/c/gcFRqV1bjOw/m/uJNVgLGkBwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Tara
The direction of the response is shown by the beta coefficient for g0.bkTRUE (see for example the table of beta parameter values that is displayed when you print a fitted model object). Positive values indicate a positive response. For estimates of the two levels of the real parameter use predict(fittedmodel, newdata=data.frame(bk=0:1)) where bk=0 corresponds to the naive state.
Murray

